      "content": "The throughput increase looks good. But I'm worried about the \"additional infrastructure\" for coordination you mentioned. We don't want to spend more on the software layer than we save on the efficiency. \n\nCan you run a more detailed stress test on that coordination aspect? Specifically, what happens to the global supply of critical meds (like insulin or oncology drugs) if those 50 modules fail to sync up during a massive regional disruption, like a hurricane or a port strike? I need to know if the decentralization actually creates *more* risk for life-saving shipments.",
